================================================================================
Build -> Objects: analytics tables listed under Unity Catalog when grouped by source
================================================================================

Context:
In Graph -> Build -> Objects, the "By source" view showed "Analytics" as its own
group, next to Lakebase (Postgres) / Unity Catalog / Triple store. Analytics is a
usage, not a source: the analytics job output tables are Unity Catalog tables.
Sources are now only Lakebase (Postgres), Unity Catalog or Neo4j. The "By usage"
view keeps its Analytics bucket.

Changes:
1. src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/BuildObjects.py
   - _analytics_groups replaced by _with_analytics: appends the version's
     analytics items (last, drop-safe) to the Unity Catalog group; a failed
     scan adds its reason to that group's error instead of a separate group.
     When the analytics schema differs, the group location lists both.
   - Delta backend: the "Triple store" group is now "Unity Catalog"
     (key unity_catalog), with the analytics tables merged into it.
   - Lakebase backend: analytics merged into the Unity Catalog (sync) group.
2. tests/units/dtwin/test_build_objects.py
   - Delta and scan-error tests updated to the single Unity Catalog group;
     new test for the Lakebase merge (items and combined location).
3. docs/user-guide.md
   - Objects tab: "by source" groups listed; analytics sit in Unity Catalog.

Modified files:
- src/back/objects/digitaltwin/build/BuildObjects.py
- tests/units/dtwin/test_build_objects.py
- docs/user-guide.md
